# Food and the house as chains (doc 62 phase 7): one asks what the other's eating, or says what they think of a dish,
# or tells a trouble with the house; the other answers as they are (food.answer, food.opinion, home.answer,
# home.advice), and the talk may close in kind (keeping.sorry, keeping.glad, keeping.nod). Every reply is the
# replier's own best rule, so one question has dozens of answers.

# ================================================================ FOOD: asking, telling, claiming

rule e1_fd_ask_supper
when concept=talk.food pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family|spouses|apprentice
cooldown 1d
say What's for #supper#, then? | Eaten yet today? | What are you having tonight? | Had anything good to eat lately?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_supper_dusk
when concept=talk.food here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 1d
say Off home to your #supper#? | Smells like everyone's cooking but me. What are you having? | Is there a pot on at yours?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_cook
when concept=talk.food other.job=cook|baker|innkeeper|brewer
cooldown 2d
say What's good at yours today? | What's on the fire today, then? | Anything worth coming in for today?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_pup
when concept=talk.food self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Have you had your dinner, #address#? | Eaten your greens? | What did your mother give you for breakfast?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_neighbour
when concept=talk.food pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 2d
say Something smelled grand through the wall last night. What was it? | Was that you frying at midnight? | Your chimney's been going all day. What are you cooking?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_claim_bread
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 1d
say Warm bread and butter. Nothing in the realm beats it. | A pie's only as good as its crust. | Stew's better the second day. Everyone knows that. | Cheese and an apple. That's a meal.
then other: food.opinion

scene e1_fd_claim_raw
when topic=food
cooldown 2d
a : Cooked meat's all very well, but some days a wolf wants a bone with the red still on it. | I'd eat a rabbit whole if nobody was looking. | My grandfather said fire ruins good meat.
b[piety=devout] : The fire's a gift. Don't spit on it.
b[job=cook] : Then what am I for? Go and chew a sheep.
b[stage=young] : I ate a beetle once. Is that the same?
b[humour=merry|dry] : Don't tell the cook. Tell me, and bring two.
b : Hush. Somebody'll hear. | Fur and all? | Your grandfather had no teeth by fifty, I'll bet.
a?[humour=merry] : I'm only half joking. The other half's hungry.
a : We're none of us so civilised as we look. | Fur and all. | He had all of them. He bit a magistrate.

rule e1_fd_claim_fish
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say Fish is better than meat. There. I've said it. | A fresh herring's worth any roast. | Give me a trout over a chop, every time.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_sweet
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say A meal's not done without something sweet after. | Honey cake. If I'm ever rich, I'll eat it every day. | Plum jam on everything. Everything.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_drink
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say Cider's better than ale and I'll hear no argument. | A meal without ale is just eating. | Water's for washing. Supper wants a cup of something.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_pie
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say What goes in a pie? Anything. That's the beauty of a pie. | Pork pie, cold, on a step in the sun. That's happiness. | Never trust a pie with a soft bottom.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_onions
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say Everything starts with an onion. Everything good. | Turnips are nobody's favourite. Name one wolf. | Too much salt ruins a stew. Too little ruins a cook.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_merry
when concept=talk.food humour=merry
cooldown 2d
say If I ate how I wanted, I'd be banned from every tavern in the realm. | I've decided gravy is a drink. | My diet is simple. Whatever's nearest.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_old
when concept=talk.food stage=old
cooldown 2d
say Food tasted of something when I was young. | You pups don't know what a real pie is. | We ate what we were given and we said thank you.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_cook
when concept=talk.food job=cook
cooldown 2d
say Nobody salts enough. Nobody. | People think cooking's fire. It's patience. | If one more wolf asks for it rare, I'll serve them the cow.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_baker
when concept=talk.food job=baker
cooldown 2d
say Bread's a whole meal on its own. Fight me. | You can tell a town by its bread. | Day-old bread's for toasting. Not for complaining about.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_brewer
when concept=talk.food job=brewer|innkeeper
cooldown 2d
say A good ale is food, you know. Barley. Practically bread. | The new barrel's the best I've had in years. | Folk don't drink like they used to. Thank the gods.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_fisher
when concept=talk.food job=fisher|sailor
cooldown 2d
say Folk who won't eat fish have never had one an hour out of the water. | Salt fish and hard bread kept me alive a whole season. | Fish heads make the best soup. Don't pull that face.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_farmer
when concept=talk.food job=farmer|herder
cooldown 2d
say Town folk think eggs come from a basket. | Grow it yourself and it tastes twice as good. | Nobody thanks the farmer at the feast.
then other: food.opinion

## The realm's dishes, where you stand

rule e1_fd_claim_fens
when concept=talk.food here.region=fens
cooldown 2d
say No fish like an eel. Fight me. | Jellied eel on Restday. That's the Fens. | The eel traps were heaving this morning.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_larkfield
when concept=talk.food here.region=larkfield
cooldown 2d
say Downs mutton. They talk about it in Ridgemere. | Mutton stew with barley. Nothing better on a #cold# night. | The cheese up the downs is the best in the realm.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_southmeadow
when concept=talk.food here.region=southmeadow
cooldown 2d
say Our wine's wasted on the north. They put honey in it. | Figs, peaches, plums. Where else would you live? | The orchards are dropping fruit faster than we can pick.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_frosthollow
when concept=talk.food here.region=frosthollow
cooldown 2d
say Smoked fish and black bread. Food that knows it's winter. | A miner's pasty. Eat it with your paws and your eyes shut. | Nothing goes off up here. The cold sees to it.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_coldwater
when concept=talk.food here.region=lake
cooldown 2d
say Glasswater trout. The rest of the realm eats mud by comparison. | Lake char, smoked over juniper. Have you had it? | Clean water, sweet fish. That's the secret.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_oakhaven
when concept=talk.food here.region=woods
cooldown 2d
say Mushrooms and venison. The woods feed you, if you know them. | Wild boar, slow roasted. Ask anyone in Oakhaven. | Hazelnuts in the bread. That's how we do it.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_ridgemere
when concept=talk.food here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 2d
say Ridgemere's a fish city. Herring, mussels, crab. | Best thing in this city's the chowder off the wharf. | Everything in this city tastes faintly of the sea.
then other: food.opinion

## The year as it falls on the table

rule e1_fd_season_winter
when concept=talk.food here.season=winter
cooldown 1d
say Turnips again. I'd give a tooth for a fresh pea. | Salt pork, salt fish, salt everything. | The cellar's half empty and it's not midwinter.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_season_spring
when concept=talk.food here.season=spring
cooldown 1d
say First greens of the year! Nettles three days running. | Lamb's on the market. Spring's here. | The hens are laying again. Eggs with everything.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_season_summer
when concept=talk.food here.season=summer
cooldown 1d
say Strawberries at the market. Ate them before I got home. | Too hot to light a fire. Cold meat and pickles. | Peas, fresh from the pod. Like eating sunshine.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_season_autumn
when concept=talk.food here.season=autumn
cooldown 1d
say Blackberries in every hedge. My paws are purple. | Harvest supper's soon. I'm saving room. | Pig-killing time. Sausages for weeks.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_festival
when concept=talk.food here.day=festival
cooldown 1d
say Have you tried the roast? Go, before it's gone. | They've a whole ox turning on the square. | I've eaten three of everything. I'm starting on four.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_restday_fast
when concept=talk.food here.day=rest piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say Fasting till the bell. My belly's praying louder than I am. | No food till after chapel. The gods test us. | I keep the fast. Mostly. There was a biscuit.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_fd_tavern
when concept=talk.food here.place=tavern
cooldown 1d
say The pie here's better than it has any right to be. | Don't have the fish. Trust me. | Whatever the cook's done to that stew, it's working.
then other: food.opinion

## Telling them, unasked

rule e1_fd_tell_poor
when concept=talk.food wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Bread and water till Fiveday. | I can make one onion last three days. It's an art. | I bought the bones the butcher was throwing out. Soup for a week.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fd_tell_hungry
when concept=talk.food hungry=yes
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say I've not eaten since yesterday morning. | Don't say pie. Don't say anything. | My belly's been growling at strangers.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fd_tell_dole
when concept=talk.food on_dole=yes
cooldown 2d
say The parish soup's water with a rumour of leek. | Parish bread again. I'm grateful. I'm sick of it. | They gave us dole cheese. Hard as a paving stone.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fd_tell_rich
when concept=talk.food wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say Our new cook's from Southmeadow. You can taste the sun in her sauces. | We had a pheasant at dinner. Nobody liked it but me. | I've a cellar of wine I'll never drink through.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_fd_tell_spouse
when concept=talk.food self.spouse
cooldown 2d
say #self.spouse# cooked last night. Something new. I'm still not sure what. | #self.spouse# hides the honey from me. I always find it. | #self.spouse# makes the best dumplings in town. Don't tell my mother.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_fd_tell_child
when concept=talk.food self.child
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# won't eat anything green. Anything. | #self.child# ate a whole loaf on the way home from the baker. | #self.child# made me breakfast. I ate it. I'm brave.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_fd_tell_widowed
when concept=talk.food widowed=yes
cooldown 2d
say I still cook for two. Habit. The neighbours eat well. | Nobody to cook for. I just eat bread now. | Their stew. I can't get it right. I keep trying.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fd_tell_working
when concept=talk.food working=yes shift=during
cooldown 2d
say Haven't stopped for a bite since dawn. | I'll eat when it's done. If it's ever done. | Crust in my pocket. Lunch.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_fd_tell_travelling
when concept=talk.food travelling=yes
cooldown 1d
say Road food. Hard cheese and harder bread. | Every inn on the road does the same stew. Same stew! | I've eaten in nine taverns this month. One was good.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_fd_tell_sump
when concept=talk.food quarter=sump
cooldown 2d
say Eel heads by the Sump steps. Penny a bag. Don't ask. | Twenty to one hearth in our building. You cook when you can. | The tide brought in a crate of cabbages. We ate like lords.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fd_tell_heights
when concept=talk.food quarter=heights
cooldown 2d
say Another dinner on the Heights. Nine courses. I'll burst. | They served snails. I said they were lovely. They weren't. | Our cook won't speak to me since I asked for plain mutton.
then other: keeping.nod

## A pie promised, between friends

scene e1_fd_promise_pie
when topic=food pair.band=friends|family
once per other
remember pair: pie_promised 7d
a : I'll bake you a pie this week. Hold me to it. | Come by on Restday. I'll make a stew big enough for two. | I owe you a supper. I've not forgotten.
b[warmth=cold] : If you like. | If you must. | Don't trouble yourself.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : You're a good friend. I'll not say no. | I'll bring the bread. Such as it is. | I'll not pretend I don't need it.
b[humour=merry] : I'm holding you to it in front of witnesses. | I'll come hungry. Very hungry. | I'll remind you every day till you do.
b[stage=young] : A whole pie? For me? | Is there pudding? | Can I bring my brother?
b : I'll hold you to that. | I'll be there. | I'll believe it when I smell it.
a : Hold me, then. | Bring a big bowl. | Fair.

rule e1_fd_pie_owed
when concept=talk.food pair.mem.pie_promised
cooldown 2d
say About that pie we talked of. Is it happening? | That supper. I've not forgotten. I've just not done it. | I've been thinking about that stew all week.
then other: keeping.nod

# ================================================================ FOOD: the answer (self answers what they eat)

rule e1_fa_plain
when concept=food.answer
say Bread and whatever's in the pot. | Stew. It's always stew. | Not much. A bit of cheese. | Whatever I can find, when I get in.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_plain2
when concept=food.answer
say Porridge, a bit of bacon if I'm lucky. | Soup, bread, bed. | Haven't decided. Something with onions.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_poor
when concept=food.answer wealth=poor
say Turnip broth. Again. | Bread and dripping. Same as yesterday. | A heel of cheese and hope.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fa_destitute
when concept=food.answer wealth=destitute
priority 1
say Nothing yet. Maybe nothing at all. | Whatever the baker throws out at dusk. | I've a crust. That's my day.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fa_rich
when concept=food.answer wealth=rich
say Duck, I think. Or goose. Cook decides. | Venison with a plum sauce. Quite nice. | We've guests, so something grand. I'll eat bread in the kitchen after.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_fa_hungry
when concept=food.answer hungry=yes
priority 2
say Nothing! Don't even ask. | I've not eaten since yesterday. | Don't talk about food. I'll cry.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fa_dole
when concept=food.answer on_dole=yes
priority 1
say The parish loaf. All of it, in one go. | Dole soup. It's soup, near enough. | Whatever the chapel's giving.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fa_homeless
when concept=food.answer homeless=yes
priority 2
say Nothing to cook on, nowhere to cook it. | What I'm given. | A crust from the tavern back door.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fa_cook
when concept=food.answer job=cook
say I cooked for thirty today. I'll eat bread and cheese standing up. | Whatever's left in the pot. Burnt bits. Best bits. | Nothing. Cooks don't eat. Didn't you know?
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_baker
when concept=food.answer job=baker
say Bread. What else? Yesterday's, mind. | The loaves that came out wrong. | A bun. A big one. I earned it.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_brewer
when concept=food.answer job=brewer
say Bread and ale. It's barley twice over. | Whatever goes with the new barrel. | Tasting, mostly. It counts.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_innkeeper
when concept=food.answer job=innkeeper
say Whatever the guests didn't finish. Don't tell them. | The stew. I always eat the stew. I know what's in it. | Nothing till the last one's gone home.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_fisher
when concept=food.answer job=fisher|sailor
say Fish. Always fish. Happy with fish. | The ones too small to sell. Sweetest. | Salt herring and a heel of bread.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_farmer
when concept=food.answer job=farmer
say Eggs. The hens won't stop. | Our own peas, our own pork. Can't beat it. | Whatever we didn't sell at market.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_herder
when concept=food.answer job=herder
say Mutton. Not any I knew, I hope. | Curds and bread out on the hill. | Porridge. Herders eat porridge. Lamb's for selling.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_guard
when concept=food.answer job=guard|soldier
say Barracks porridge. Thick enough to stop an arrow. | Sausage and bread, eaten on the walk. | Whatever's left when the night watch is done with it.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_miner
when concept=food.answer job=miner
say A pasty, eaten in the dark. | Something hot, if there's any left when I'm up. | Whatever's not got rock dust in it.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_woodcutter
when concept=food.answer job=woodcutter|laborer
say Enough for three. I've been swinging an axe all day. | Bread, cheese, a raw onion. Laborer's dinner. | Anything. Everything. Twice.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_servant
when concept=food.answer job=servant
say What comes back from the family's table. | The kitchen gets the ends. I like the ends. | Bread and dripping in the scullery. Standing up.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_priest
when concept=food.answer job=priest
say Whatever my flock sends round. Tonight, a pie. | Plain food. The gods like plain. | A widow sent me a cake. I mustn't say it was dry.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_young
when concept=food.answer stage=young
say Porridge. I hate porridge. | Bread and jam! Mostly jam. | I don't know. Mother won't say. Something with cabbage.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_old
when concept=food.answer stage=old
say Soft things. My teeth have retired. | Broth, bread soaked in it. Same as every night. | Not much. You eat less, at my age.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_spouse
when concept=food.answer self.spouse
cooldown 1d
say #self.spouse#'s cooking, so something burnt. | Whatever #self.spouse# has on. I don't ask. | #self.spouse#'s famous dumplings. Famous in our house.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_fa_child
when concept=food.answer self.child
cooldown 1d
say Whatever #self.child# leaves on the plate. | #self.child# says it's soup tonight. #self.child# made it. Gods help me. | Bread. #self.child# ate everything else.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_fa_widowed
when concept=food.answer widowed=yes
say I cook for one now. Still make too much. | Bread and cheese. I can't be bothered for one. | Their stew. I'm learning it.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fa_working
when concept=food.answer working=yes shift=during
say Haven't stopped long enough to think. | Bread in my pocket. Eaten standing. | Later. If there's a later.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_travelling
when concept=food.answer travelling=yes
say Whatever the next inn's got. | Road cheese. It's a kind of cheese. | Hard bread and an apple, walking.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_devout_rest
when concept=food.answer piety=devout here.day=rest
say Nothing till the bell. It's Restday. | I'm fasting. Ask me after chapel. | A crust and a prayer.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_short
when concept=food.answer temper=short
say Why does everyone want to know what I eat? | Food. I'll be eating food. | My business.

rule e1_fa_merry
when concept=food.answer humour=merry
cooldown 1d
say Three suppers, one after the other. | Whatever's not nailed down. | A pie inside a pie. I'm working on the idea.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_fa_heights
when concept=food.answer quarter=heights
say Eight courses. One of them a jelly with a fish in it. | Something French- No. Something Southmeadow. Very small. | Dinner at the Merriots'. I'll be hungry after.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_sump
when concept=food.answer quarter=sump
say Whatever's cheap at the Sump steps. | Eel heads, boiled. They grow on you. | Whatever the tide brings.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_fa_winter
when concept=food.answer here.season=winter
say Salt pork and the last of the turnips. | Pease pudding. It's been on since dawn. | Broth, and lots of it.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_spring
when concept=food.answer here.season=spring
say Nettle soup. It's the hungry gap. | Eggs. The hens are back at it. | The last of the cellar and the first of the greens.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_summer
when concept=food.answer here.season=summer
say Bread and cheese. Too hot to cook. | Peas, raw from the pod. | Cold mutton and a cucumber.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_autumn
when concept=food.answer here.season=autumn
say Apples with everything. | Sausages. Pig-killing week. | Blackberry and apple. The pie, I mean.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_fens
when concept=food.answer here.region=fens
say Eel. What else? | Duck, if my sling was true. | Eel pie. My mother's eel pie.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_frosthollow
when concept=food.answer here.region=frosthollow
say Smoked fish and black bread. | Oats and mutton fat. Keeps the cold out. | Whatever keeps. Which up here is everything.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_coldwater
when concept=food.answer here.region=lake
say Trout. Fried in butter. | Char off the boats this morning. | A fish I caught off the jetty. Proud of it.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_oakhaven
when concept=food.answer here.region=woods
say Mushrooms on toast. I picked them myself. | Rabbit. Somebody's snare was generous. | Venison stew. The hunters had a good week.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_larkfield
when concept=food.answer here.region=larkfield
say Mutton. You're in Larkfield. | Mutton and barley. Mutton and turnip. Mutton. | Downs cheese and an apple.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_southmeadow
when concept=food.answer here.region=southmeadow
say Bread, olives, a peach. A cup of wine. | Plums. I'm sick of plums. Don't tell anyone. | Something with figs. Everything has figs.
then other: food.react

rule e1_fa_ridgemere
when concept=food.answer here.region=ridgemere
say Herring. This city floats on herring. | A bucket of mussels off the wharf. | A pie from the stall by the steps.
then other: food.react

# ================================================================ FOOD: hearing what they eat (self reacts)

rule e1_fr_plain
when concept=food.react
say Sounds good. | Could be worse. | Save me some. | Lucky you. | Can't beat it.

rule e1_fr_plain2
when concept=food.react
say Mm. I'd eat that. | Same as me, near enough. | That'll keep you going. | Not bad at all.

rule e1_fr_hungry
when concept=food.react hungry=yes
priority 1
say Stop. My belly heard that. | I'd fight you for it. | Don't. I've not eaten.

rule e1_fr_poor
when concept=food.react wealth=poor|destitute
say Better than mine. | I'd swap you in a heartbeat. | That's a feast, where I'm sat.

rule e1_fr_rich
when concept=food.react wealth=rich
say How... hearty. | I've always wondered what that tastes like. | Quite right. Simple is best. So they say.

rule e1_fr_warm
when concept=food.react warmth=warm
say Come and have yours at mine one night. | Oh, that sounds lovely. | Bring it round and we'll share.
remember pair: pie_promised 7d

rule e1_fr_merry
when concept=food.react humour=merry
say And for afters? Another one? | I'll be round at the smell. | Put my name on a bowl.

rule e1_fr_dry
when concept=food.react humour=dry
say Living like a lord. | They'll write songs about it. | Steady, now.

rule e1_fr_short
when concept=food.react temper=short
say Right. | Good for you. | I didn't really want to know.

rule e1_fr_cook
when concept=food.react job=cook|baker
say I'd have done it with more salt. | Who cooked it? I want to know. | Not bad. Mine's better.

rule e1_fr_old
when concept=food.react stage=old
say We'd have called that a feast, in my day. | Mind you chew it. | That's what my mother made.

rule e1_fr_young
when concept=food.react stage=young
say Can I have some? | Is there pudding? | I'd rather have cake.

# ================================================================ FOOD: an opinion (self answers a remark on food)

rule e1_fo_plain
when concept=food.opinion
say #agree#. Can't argue with that. | Depends who's cooking. | Now you've made me hungry. | You and your belly.

rule e1_fo_plain2
when concept=food.opinion
say Hm. Maybe. | I'll take your word for it. | There's worse things to think about. | Speak for yourself.

rule e1_fo_disagree
when concept=food.opinion honesty=frank
say No. Wrong. Completely wrong. | That's daft and you know it. | I've never heard such #nonsense#.

rule e1_fo_dry
when concept=food.opinion humour=dry
say Write it on your grave. | Bold stand to take. | The gods will be relieved to know.

rule e1_fo_merry
when concept=food.opinion humour=merry
say Ha! You'd marry a pie if they'd let you. | I'll drink to that. I'll drink to anything. | Say it louder. The cook's listening.

rule e1_fo_short
when concept=food.opinion temper=short
say Do you ever talk about anything but your stomach? | Fine. Whatever you say. | I don't care what you eat.

rule e1_fo_warm
when concept=food.opinion warmth=warm
say Come and eat with us one night. I'll prove you right or wrong. | Oh, you'll have to try my mother's. | I'll make it for you. Restday.
remember pair: pie_promised 7d

rule e1_fo_hungry
when concept=food.opinion hungry=yes
priority 1
say Stop. Please. I've not eaten. | Don't. My belly heard you. | Can we talk about something else? Anything.

rule e1_fo_poor
when concept=food.opinion wealth=poor|destitute
say I wouldn't know. I've not had it in a year. | Must be nice, having opinions about food. | Whatever's cheap is my favourite.

rule e1_fo_rich
when concept=food.opinion wealth=rich
say Our cook does it with saffron. You should try it. | Mm. I find it rather heavy. | Have it with a white wine. Changes everything.

rule e1_fo_cook
when concept=food.opinion job=cook
say Spoken like someone who's never had to cook it. | You're half right. The other half's the fire. | Come and say that in my kitchen.

rule e1_fo_baker
when concept=food.opinion job=baker
say Not without good bread, it isn't. | Ask a baker. We know. | All food's just a way of getting bread to your mouth.

rule e1_fo_old
when concept=food.opinion stage=old
say In my day we were grateful for anything. | My mother did it better. Everyone's mother did. | I've eaten for seventy years. You're half right.

rule e1_fo_young
when concept=food.opinion stage=young
say Ew. | Only if there's honey on it. | I'd rather have cake.

rule e1_fo_devout
when concept=food.opinion piety=devout
say Give thanks for it, whatever it is. | The gods gave us the fire for a reason. | Gluttony's a sin, you know. Pass it here.

rule e1_fo_spouses
when concept=food.opinion pair.band=spouses
say You burned it the last time, #dear#. | You say that every night. | Then cook it for me.

rule e1_fo_from_fens
when concept=food.opinion from=mirebridge
say Not compared to an eel. | You've never had a Fen supper. | Back home, we'd put eel in it.

rule e1_fo_from_south
when concept=food.opinion from=southmeadow
say It wants fruit in it. Everything does. | Back home we'd have it with wine. | Not like at home. Nothing is.

rule e1_fo_from_north
when concept=food.opinion from=frosthollow|coldwater
say We'd smoke it, up north. | Smoked is better. Everything's better smoked. | Wants more fat. For the cold.

rule e1_fo_from_larkfield
when concept=food.opinion from=larkfield
say Better with mutton. | Can't beat a downs supper. | Have you tried it with mint?

rule e1_fo_from_ridgemere
when concept=food.opinion from=ridgemere
say Better with a bit of fish in it. | Wants rain on it, like at home. | City folk know food. Fight me.

# ================================================================ HOME: asking, troubles, telling

rule e1_hm_ask_house
when concept=talk.home pair.band=acquaintances|friends|apprentice|family
cooldown 1d
say How's the house? | Keeping the roof on? | All well at home? | How's your place these days?
then other: home.answer

rule e1_hm_ask_new
when concept=talk.home pair.band=strangers|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say Where is it you live? | You're near here, aren't you? | Is it a good street, yours?
then other: home.answer

rule e1_hm_ask_weather
when concept=talk.home here.weather=rain|storm|snow
cooldown 1d
say Is your roof holding in this? | Mine's leaking like a sieve. Yours? | Dry at yours, I hope?
then other: home.answer

rule e1_hm_roof
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 2d
say My roof's leaking again. | There's a drip over the bed I can't find. | Lost two slates in the wind.
then other: home.advice
remember self: roof_leaks 3d

rule e1_hm_roof_still
when concept=talk.home self.mem.roof_leaks
cooldown 2d
say Still leaking. I've a pot in every room now. | The roof again. I can hear it in my sleep. | I mended the roof. It's leaking somewhere new.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_chimney
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 2d
say My chimney smokes. I'm cured like a ham. | The fire won't draw. Smoke everywhere. | There's something nesting in the chimney.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_damp
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 2d
say Damp's coming up the walls again. | Everything I own smells of mould. | There's a green patch on the ceiling. It's growing.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_mice
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 2d
say Mice in the larder again. | Something's chewing in the walls at night. | A rat ran over my foot in my own kitchen.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_door
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 2d
say The door's swollen. Won't shut. | My shutter's off its hinge. | The step's cracked right through.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_furniture
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 2d
say The chair's lost a leg. I'm sitting on a crate. | My bed broke. In the night. With me in it. | The table wobbles. Soup everywhere.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_wood
when concept=talk.home here.season=autumn|winter
cooldown 2d
say The woodpile's half what it should be. | I'm burning wet wood. The smoke! | Firewood's dear this year.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_hens
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 3d
say The hens have stopped laying. | A fox had one of my hens. | My hens keep roosting in the kitchen.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_noise
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 2d
say The neighbours shouted all night. | There's a baby next door that never sleeps. | Somebody on my stair's learning the drum.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_lodger
when concept=talk.home
cooldown 3d
say My lodger's not paid in a month. | The lodger's started cooking fish in his room. | I need a lodger. The rent's too much on my own.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_hm_moving
when concept=talk.home drive=restless|ambitious
cooldown 3d
say I'm thinking of moving. Anywhere. | I've seen a house I want. I can't afford it. Yet. | This street's too small for me.
then other: home.advice

## Telling, unasked

rule e1_hm_tell_rent
when concept=talk.home wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Rent's due and I'm short. Again. | The landlord's put it up. Third time. | I pay half my wages for one room.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_hm_tell_owes
when concept=talk.home owes=yes
cooldown 2d
say The landlord's man was at the door again. | I've not paid the rent. I go in by the back. | If they put me out, I don't know where I'll go.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_hm_tell_homeless
when concept=talk.home homeless=yes
cooldown 1d
priority 2
say I've nowhere, #address#. Not a room. | Doorways and haylofts. That's my home now. | I used to have a door I could shut.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_hm_tell_rich
when concept=talk.home wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say We're having a new wing built. The noise! | I've bought the house next door. For the garden. | New glass in every window. You should see it shine.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_hm_tell_heights
when concept=talk.home quarter=heights
cooldown 2d
say The Heights are all scaffolding this season. Everyone's building. | Our neighbours have a new carriage house. Ours is older. | Eleven rooms and I can never find my spectacles.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_sump
when concept=talk.home quarter=sump
cooldown 2d
say The tide came up through the floor. We sleep on the table. | Twenty to a stair in our building. | There's a crack in our wall you can put your arm through.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_hm_tell_wharf
when concept=talk.home quarter=wharf|docks
cooldown 2d
say The gulls are on my roof at dawn, every dawn. | My room smells of tar and fish. I don't notice any more. | The tide slaps under my floor all night.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_works
when concept=talk.home quarter=works
cooldown 2d
say Soot on the sill, soot on the bread, soot on me. | The kilns keep my walls warm. Too warm. | You can't hang washing up at the Works. It comes in grey.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_spouse
when concept=talk.home self.spouse
cooldown 2d
say #self.spouse# moved all the furniture again. | #self.spouse# wants a bigger house. Wants. | #self.spouse# fixed the shelf. It's on the floor now.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_child
when concept=talk.home self.child
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# swept the whole floor without being asked. I nearly fainted. | #self.child# has dug a hole in the yard. A big one. Why? | #self.child# wants a room of their own. Don't we all.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_hm_tell_widowed
when concept=talk.home widowed=yes
cooldown 2d
say The house is too quiet now. | I keep their chair by the fire. | I don't like going home in the evenings.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_hm_tell_old
when concept=talk.home stage=old
cooldown 2d
say The stairs get longer every year. | I've lived in my house fifty years. I'll leave it feet first. | My pups want me to move in with them. Not likely.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_young
when concept=talk.home stage=young
cooldown 2d
say I've got a den. It's secret. I can't say where. | I'm sleeping in the loft now! With the apples! | My brother kicks in his sleep.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_servant
when concept=talk.home job=servant
cooldown 2d
say I keep a house that isn't mine, and sleep under its stairs. | Scrubbed their floors all day. Mine can wait. | The family's having the parlour done. Guess who's carrying the furniture.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_winter
when concept=talk.home here.season=winter
cooldown 1d
say Ice inside the window this morning. | I sleep in my coat. And my boots. | The water froze in the jug. Indoors.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_spring
when concept=talk.home here.season=spring
cooldown 1d
say Turned the house out for spring. The fur under the bed! | Beat the rugs till my arm dropped off. | Shutters open at last. The house can breathe.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_summer
when concept=talk.home here.season=summer
cooldown 1d
say House is like an oven. Slept in the yard. | Flies in every room. | Shutters shut all day, or we cook.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_autumn
when concept=talk.home here.season=autumn
cooldown 1d
say Got the gutters cleared before the rain. Just. | Woodpile's stacked to the eaves. Winter can come. | Apples drying on every shelf in the house.
then other: keeping.glad

## A ladder lent, between neighbours

# ================================================================ HOME: the answer (self answers about their house)

rule e1_ha_plain
when concept=home.answer
say Standing, which is all you can ask. | Much the same. Roof on, door shut. | Can't complain. Well. The damp. | It's home. It'll do.

rule e1_ha_plain2
when concept=home.answer
say Warm, dry, mostly. | Small, but mine. | There's always something. This week it's the step.

rule e1_ha_poor
when concept=home.answer wealth=poor
say Roof leaks and the rent's up. | One room, one window. It does. | I'd be fine if the landlord died. I'm joking. Mostly.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_ha_destitute
when concept=home.answer wealth=destitute
priority 1
say I'll be out by Fiveday if I can't pay. | Sold the table. Sold the chairs. Still short. | Don't ask. Please.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_ha_homeless
when concept=home.answer homeless=yes
priority 3
say I've no house, #address#. | Under the bridge, tonight. | Wherever's dry.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_ha_owes
when concept=home.answer owes=yes
priority 1
say Behind on the rent. Don't tell anyone. | I go in by the back door now. Collector. | It's a roof. For now.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_ha_rich
when concept=home.answer wealth=rich
say Very well. We've had the hall done. | Splendid. New hangings from Southmeadow. | Too big, honestly. I lose the servants.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_ha_heights
when concept=home.answer quarter=heights
say Eleven rooms and nothing to do in any of them. | Lovely view. Dreadful neighbours. | The fountain's broken. A great trial.

rule e1_ha_sump
when concept=home.answer quarter=sump
say Damp. It's the Sump. | The water's in the cellar again. And the rats. | Three families on our stair. It's lively.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_ha_harbour_hill
when concept=home.answer quarter=harbour_hill
say Four flights up and worth it. You can see the whole Sound. | My knees hate it. My eyes love it. | Steep. Everything's steep.

rule e1_ha_wharf
when concept=home.answer quarter=wharf|docks
say Gulls on the roof, tide under the floor. | Smells of tar. I've stopped noticing. | Noisy. The carts start before dawn.

rule e1_ha_works
when concept=home.answer quarter=works
say Warm, from the kilns. Sooty, from the kilns. | Grey. Everything's grey. | Fine, if you don't breathe much.

rule e1_ha_commons
when concept=home.answer quarter=commons|suburbs|office
say Quiet street, nobody bothers us. Can't ask more. | Two rooms and a yard. We're content. | Neighbours are decent. That's half of it.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_ha_spouse
when concept=home.answer self.spouse
cooldown 1d
say #self.spouse# keeps moving the furniture. I keep finding it. | #self.spouse# wants it painted. I want my supper. | Fine. #self.spouse# keeps it nice. I keep out of the way.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_ha_child
when concept=home.answer self.child
cooldown 1d
say #self.child# has drawn on every wall I own. | Loud. #self.child# has found a drum. | Full of #self.child#'s things. I live in the corner.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_ha_widowed
when concept=home.answer widowed=yes
say Too big. Too quiet. | I keep their chair where it was. | Tidy. Nobody to make a mess.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_ha_old
when concept=home.answer stage=old
say The stairs and I aren't speaking. | Same house fifty years. Same creaks. | My bones and the walls, both settling.

rule e1_ha_young
when concept=home.answer stage=young
say I share a bed with my brother. He kicks. | I've a den under the stairs! | Loud. Mother shouts a lot.

rule e1_ha_crafter
when concept=home.answer job=crafter|smith|laborer
say I mend everyone's house but mine. | Made the table myself. It wobbles. | Fine. I fixed the roof. Myself. With help from gravity.

rule e1_ha_innkeeper
when concept=home.answer job=innkeeper
say I live over the taproom. I've not slept in ten years. | Full of strangers, as ever. | Every room let and I'm on the bench.

rule e1_ha_servant
when concept=home.answer job=servant
say I live in someone else's house. I've a cupboard under the stairs. | Theirs is lovely. Mine's a cot. | Spotless. Not mine, mind.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule e1_ha_farmer
when concept=home.answer job=farmer|herder
say The house is fine. The byre's falling down. | Hens in the kitchen again. | The roof wants thatching and the field wants me.
then other: home.advice

rule e1_ha_priest
when concept=home.answer job=priest
say The manse is cold as charity. | I've a room behind the chapel. It suits me. | Full of other people's troubles.

rule e1_ha_restless
when concept=home.answer drive=restless
say I'd move tomorrow, if I had somewhere to go. | Same four walls. Same four walls. | Fine. Dull. Fine.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_ha_cold
when concept=home.answer warmth=cold
say It's a house. Walls, roof. | Fine. | Why?

rule e1_ha_merry
when concept=home.answer humour=merry
cooldown 1d
say Still standing! Mostly by habit. | It's a palace. A small, damp, leaning palace. | The roof leaks, but only on the landlord's side.
then other: keeping.glad

rule e1_ha_winter
when concept=home.answer here.season=winter
say Cold. I can't keep the fire in. | Snug, if you sit in the hearth. | Ice on the inside of the window.

rule e1_ha_summer
when concept=home.answer here.season=summer
say Hot as an oven. Shutters shut all day. | Flies. Everywhere, flies. | Close. Can't sleep for the heat.

rule e1_ha_fens
when concept=home.answer here.region=fens
say The river's at the bottom step. | Damp to the rafters. Fen house. | Leaning a little more each year. Like me.

rule e1_ha_frosthollow
when concept=home.answer here.region=frosthollow
say Snow to the eaves, fire in the middle. | Thick walls. Thick as a mountain. | Warm, if you keep the door shut.

rule e1_ha_coldwater
when concept=home.answer here.region=lake
say I can hear the lake from my bed. | Mist under the door every dawn. | Damp, but you can see Glasswater.

rule e1_ha_oakhaven
when concept=home.answer here.region=woods
say An oak's dropping branches on my roof. | Roots are lifting the floor. | Snug under the trees.

rule e1_ha_larkfield
when concept=home.answer here.region=larkfield
say The wind off the downs has half my thatch. | Sheep in the yard again. | Old walls, thick and dry. Can't fault it.

rule e1_ha_southmeadow
when concept=home.answer here.region=southmeadow
say Cool as a cellar, shutters closed. | Grapes over the door. Lizards on the wall. | Hot. It's always hot.

rule e1_ha_ridgemere
when concept=home.answer here.region=ridgemere
say Damp. It's Ridgemere. | The rain comes in sideways under the door. | Everything I own smells of the sea.

# ================================================================ HOME: advice (self answers a trouble with the house)

rule e1_hv_plain
when concept=home.advice
say Put a pot under it and pray. | That's houses for you. | Leave it till spring. Everyone does. | Sounds like a job for someone else.

rule e1_hv_plain2
when concept=home.advice
say Mine's the same. | Get a man in. Or a wolf. | Have you tried hitting it?

rule e1_hv_crafter
when concept=home.advice job=crafter|smith
say I'll come and look at it. Bring me a pie. | Ten minutes with the right tool. I'll lend you the tool. | Don't touch it. You'll make it worse. I'll come round.
remember pair: offered_help 7d

rule e1_hv_laborer
when concept=home.advice job=laborer|woodcutter
say Give me a ladder and a morning. | I'll do it for a penny and a cup of ale. | I've a strong back and a free Restday.
remember pair: offered_help 7d

rule e1_hv_neighbour
when concept=home.advice pair.neighbours=yes
say Knock on my wall if you need a paw. | I'll come round after supper and look. | Borrow what you need from mine. Bring it back, mind.
remember pair: offered_help 7d

rule e1_hv_old
when concept=home.advice stage=old
say My mother swore by a rag soaked in tallow. | Same thing happened to my father's house. He moved. | In my day you mended it yourself.

rule e1_hv_young
when concept=home.advice stage=young
say I could climb up and look! | Get a cat. Cats fix everything. | Can I help? Can I hit something?

rule e1_hv_rich
when concept=home.advice wealth=rich
say Have a man in. That's what they're for. | Why not move somewhere better? | We just pay someone. It's simplest.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hv_poor
when concept=home.advice wealth=poor|destitute
say Live with it, like the rest of us. | At least you've a house to complain about. | I'd swap you.

rule e1_hv_warm
when concept=home.advice warmth=warm
say Come and stay at mine till it's done. | I'll help on Restday. Don't argue. | Poor you. Come round, I'll put the kettle on.
remember pair: offered_help 7d

rule e1_hv_cold
when concept=home.advice warmth=cold
say Not my house. | Mend it, then. | Everyone's got a leak somewhere.

rule e1_hv_merry
when concept=home.advice humour=merry
say Call it a feature. Charge the next tenant extra. | Have you tried shouting at it? Works on my brother. | Burn it down and start again. I'm joking. Half joking.

rule e1_hv_dry
when concept=home.advice humour=dry
say Look on the bright side. You'll get a new house when it falls down. | Character, that's called. | Could be worse. Could be mine.

rule e1_hv_short
when concept=home.advice temper=short
say Well, stop telling me and mend it. | Everyone's got troubles. | And what am I to do about it?

rule e1_hv_devout
when concept=home.advice piety=devout
say Have the priest bless the threshold. It helps more than you'd think. | Pray on it. Then mend it. | The gods test us in small ways too.

rule e1_hv_healer
when concept=home.advice job=healer
say Damp in the house is damp in the chest. Fix it before winter. | Burn rosemary. It clears the air. | Keep the fire up and the window cracked.

rule e1_hv_help_again
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.offered_help
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I said I'd come round. I meant it. | Still waiting for you to ask. | The offer stands. Name the day.
